<p>For a standard European flight, arriving at the terminal around two hours before departure is a comfortable buffer; for long-haul flights outside the Schengen area, closer to three hours gives room for check-in and security without rushing. If your flight is early morning, ask your driver to confirm the pickup time the evening before — traffic is lightest then, but hotel checkout and lobby wait times can still eat into the margin. Even outside peak hours, it's worth allowing a few extra minutes if your flight coincides with a weekday, since the district's office towers and the CCIB convention centre generate a steady flow of taxis, rideshares, and delivery vans along Rambla Prim and Avinguda Diagonal.</p>
